# Citation metadata for the software (Citation File Format 1.2.0). Add the arXiv identifier of the paper and the Zenodo DOI of the
# release under identifiers once they exist.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Moot Court in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Moot Court: scored, gated pre-launch forecasts of A/B test outcomes from a ledger of precedents"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark and protocol for asking what a ledger of concluded online experiments says about a proposed test before it launches:
  a ledger with admission as a status, a rolling-origin backtest over versioned snapshots, proper scores with floors and ceilings,
  calibration against a clustered null, sample-size gates, abstention, a frozen card and a weekly join that scores every card.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-05"
repository-code: "https://github.com/journey-agents/mootcourt"
url: "https://github.com/journey-agents/mootcourt"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Yingjie"
keywords:
  - online controlled experiments
  - A/B testing
  - forecasting
  - calibration
  - empirical Bayes
  - benchmark
  - abstention
